From 98f84c96cf44d9270ace824c574248e8c7618305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero <caleb@calebgj.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] lsa: --lsa loads D-LSA's index maps; qwen35 bf16 declares
 the index side

--lsa MAP reads the paper's d-lsa-weights-v1 torch zip ({L}.W_Q_idx and
{L}.W_K_idx a full-attention layer) without running its pickle, checks it
and the sizes (--lsa-window, -sink, -top-k, -top-p, -pool, -bucket,
-bucket-cap, the flat design's defaults), and gives each rank a bf16 copy
through RadBuildCtx::lsa (ABI 38, RadLsaMap; RadArchProbe::lsa_ok).

arch/common/rad_block_lsa.h declares the two KV groups (kv_lsa_idx paged
like the attention's cache, kv_lsa_bkt a page a cluster block) and the
three ops a full-attention layer; rad_block_attn_gated.h issues them after
kv_store and, where a library declares attn_paged_list, attends the decode
rows over their lists and a mixed step's prefill half densely. Without the
flag nothing is declared: arch_test's pinned graphs are unchanged.

(cherry picked from commit 2bee9f79da6e6a7f6a65640424e9fa19f47ae452)
